b:
It kind of pisses me off they insist so much on the Dracula BS with this place. Dracula wasn't real, Vlad the Impaler (the inspiration for Dracula) never set foot in this place. Bram Stoker had no idea of it as well. It's completely arbitrary. 

&nbsp;

The castle instead has historical significance with Queen Marie and the Hapsburgs. It's not that interesting of a history but for crying out loud enough with the Dracula narrative, it completely overshadowed any true history to create a cheesy, cringey tourist trap.

I watched this while I was on vacation in a major metropolitan area and it was really interesting/unnerving to look up locations as I was watching the movie and realize how close they were to where I was...

&nbsp;

It sucks that I couldn't finish it in time, and especially since it's not on a major streaming service ugh

Absolutely. A beloved animated franchise was my entire childhood. The third installment came out when I turned 18 and was headed off to college myself, resonated with me in a way I never thought possible, and I absolutely loved it because of it.

&nbsp;

When the fourth installment was announced I kind of felt like it might be ruined, but I was crying with laughter and was so happy to see another instalment. I hope they continue to make more.
